course: dictionary
lesson: 3979
title: Gait: the way we move
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A gait is the way a person or animal walks or runs: the pattern and style of their steps. You can often recognise a friend from far away by their gait, before you can see their face. Gait is a noun, so you can say a gait or some gaits.
explain: «The four main paces, called gaits, are walk, trot, canter and gallop, from slowest to fastest, each with its own pattern of legs.» The sentence shows that gaits are more than speeds. Each one has its own pattern of steps, and the words from slowest to fastest give you clues about how fast each is.
explain: Writers use gait to show what a character is like. A limping gait may suggest an injury, a swaggering gait may suggest someone proud, and a shuffling gait may suggest someone tired or unsure. Ask yourself: what does the way they walk tell me about them?
fact: Gait means the way a person or animal walks or runs.
fact: For horses, a gait is one of the ways they move: walk, trot, canter or gallop.
fact: «The four main paces, called gaits, are walk, trot, canter and gallop, from slowest to fastest.»
fact: Scientists and physiotherapists study gait to understand movement and injuries.
fact: You may meet phrases like «an uneven gait», «a slow gait» and «gait analysis».
exercise: What does gait mean? | A small gate in a fence | A loud noise made by a horse | *The way a person or animal walks or runs | A type of shoe
exercise: «The four main paces, called gaits, are walk, trot, canter and gallop, from slowest to fastest.» Which gait is the slowest? | *Walk | Gallop | Canter | Trot
exercise: Ben has a limping gait after he twisted his ankle. What does limping gait suggest? | He is very fast and full of energy | He is singing a happy song | He is a horse in a race | *He is hurt or has a sore leg
test: Which word is the noun for the way someone walks? | Grab | Gate | *Gait | Gasp
test: In horse riding, which gait is the fastest? | Canter | Trot | *Gallop | Walk
exam: A character with a swaggering gait is most likely to be: | *Proud and confident | Very hungry | Shy and nervous | Asleep and dreaming
